h(2, id: "tables") { 11. Tables }

p {
    A table is rows. A row is cells. A cell body is prose.
}

codeblock(lang: "text") {!
table {
  row(header: true) {
    cell { Name }
    cell { Kind }
  }
  row {
    cell { code{p} }
    cell { block }
  }
  row {
    cell { code{b} }
    cell { inline }
  }
}
!}

p {
    Rules checked after parse:
}

list {
    item { At least one row. }
    item { Each row has at least one cell. }
    item { Every row has the same number of cells. }
}

p {
    code{row(header: true)} emits code{<th>} instead of code{<td>}.
    code{table(caption: "...")} writes a caption.
    code{cell(colspan: 2, rowspan: 2)} sets HTML span attributes. Column counts
    are the sum of colspan values on each row; those sums must match.
}

include "fragments/sample-table.du"

h(2, id: "images") { 12. Images }

p {
    No body. First argument is the source URL or path. Optional code{alt} and
    code{href}. A non-empty href wraps the image in a link.
}

codeblock(lang: "text") {!
image("images/banner.png", alt: "DocUP")
image("images/banner.png", alt: "DocUP", href: "https://example.com")
!}

h(3, id: "figure") { 12.1 figure }

p {
    Image plus caption.
}

codeblock(lang: "text") {!
figure("images/banner.png", alt: "DocUP", caption: "The DocUP banner")
!}

p {
    An empty source is a semantic error.
}

p {
    An empty source is a semantic error. In watch mode the server maps request
    paths onto files next to the root input. Relative paths in the compiled HTML
    are resolved by the browser against the HTML file.
}

p {
    The banner at the top of this page is that block.
}
